The character-class maps, pair scores, and CJK frequency lists are derived
from src/data.rs, dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The metadata analyzer uses strict JDK charset decoders for complete fields.
It does not emulate encoding_rs decoding tables or browser-domain selection.
Names and comments use separate bounded feature profiles. Selection can
return no result; archive format declarations and fallbacks belong to callers.
Upstream continuous-text state machines are retained only as test references.

The independent-field scorer also includes IBM437, IBM850, and IBM852 byte
classifications derived from JDK mappings. These reuse the Western and
Central European pair scores; characters absent from the source models
receive neutral classes. Repeated features are capped and bounded context
summaries accumulate relative candidate support, not confidence probabilities.
